From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32-qspi: allow an explicit XIP handoff

An XIP kernel needs the QSPI controller to remain in memory-mapped mode
after U-Boot has loaded its device tree. Permit the board environment to
request that one-way handoff. The default remains to abort memory-mapped
reads, preserving the established zImage and flash-update behavior.

The variable is deliberately checked only after a successful mapped read.
The XIP boot command sets it immediately before its final SPI operation and
does not persist the environment.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 
 #include <clk.h>
 #include <dm.h>
+#include <env.h>
 #include <log.h>
 #include <reset.h>
 #include <spi.h>
@@ -353 +354,3 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
-	if (ret || mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP)
+	if (ret ||
+	    (mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP &&
+	     env_get_yesno("qspi_leave_mapped") != 1))
-- 
2.52.0
